<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">British Nationality and New Zealand Citizenship Act 1948</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1948</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The British Nationality and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> Citizenship Act 1948 created a separate New Zealand citizenship for the first time, taking effect on 1 January 1949. New Zealand citizens remained British subjects, in line with the arrangements agreed among Commonwealth countries after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>'s citizenship law of 1946. It was replaced by the Citizenship Act 1977.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/british-nationality-and-new-zealand-citizenship-act-1948.jpg" alt="British Nationality and New Zealand Citizenship Act 1948" width="320" height="297" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_New_Zealand_(1911%E2%80%931956).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
